import re,sys
def sub(path, old, new):
    s=open(path,encoding='utf-8',newline='').read()
    nl='\r\n' if '\r\n' in s else '\n'
    old=old.replace('\n',nl); new=new.replace('\n',nl)
    assert s.count(old)==1,(path,old[:40],s.count(old))
    open(path,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s.replace(old,new))
sub('configuration-loading.md',"| `nl2sql/tracing/trace.py` | the trace redactor masks every value the environment holds |\n","| `nl2sql/tracing/trace.py` | the trace redactor masks every value the environment holds |\n| `nl2sql_cli/commands/eval.py` | `CI`, so a `full` eval never runs in CI |\n| `nl2sql_cli/commands/launch.py` | `DATABASE_URL`, the one URL `nl2sql launch` offers as a candidate |\n")
sub('configuration-loading.md',"The loader remembers each file's hash so the engine can refuse to overwrite a hand edit it did not see.","The loader records the SHA-256 of `nl2sql.yaml`, each section file and each datasource file. When the engine writes one of them (saving a datasource, adding the demo), it refuses with `FILE_CHANGED` if the file on disk no longer matches, so it never overwrites a hand edit it did not see.")
sub('key-design-decisions.md',"""## The model never sees rows

We chose to give the answer model a bounded preview, the column names and the row count, over the full result. The answer writes about the data and never copies it, so the prompt does not grow with the result. Conversations and dashboards store plans and summaries, not rows.""","""## The answer model sees a preview, not the result

We chose to give the answer model a bounded preview (the first rows, the column names and the row count) over the full result, so the prompt does not grow with the result. The conversation model sees no rows at all, only each answer's summary and columns. Conversations and dashboards store plans and summaries, not rows.""")
sub('key-design-decisions.md',"jobs are short administrative work, and what a job produces is stored by the engine, so losing the list on restart loses nothing that matters.","a restart loses the job list and stops a running job, but what finished jobs produced is in the engine's stores.")
sub('conversations.md',"A run that ends `needs_clarification` ends the turn and records a pending question on the conversation. The next turn answers it with an option id (no model call) or with text the model maps to an option. A run that ends `needs_approval` ends the turn; an approver grants the request elsewhere, and the asker's `retry` re-runs the last `ask` step with no model call. See","A run that ends `needs_clarification` ends the turn and records a pending question on the conversation. The next turn answers it with an option id, which skips the conversation model, or with text the model maps to an option. A run that ends `needs_approval` ends the turn; an approver grants the request elsewhere, and the asker's `retry` re-runs the last `ask` step's question without calling the conversation model. See")
sub('access-and-security.md',", and the approver never runs the question as the asker.",". A grant runs nothing itself. It is bound to the asker and to the SQL that was asked for, so only the asker's own re-run of that SQL can use it.")
